---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Long Only Funds | The Sovereign Ledger" currentPage="products/funds/long-only">

<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10 py-8 lg:max-w-5xl">

  <!-- Breadcrumb -->
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-secondary mb-8 pt-4">
    <a href="/knowledge/aif" class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-label hover:text-primary-container transition-colors">AIF Knowledge</a>
    <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[12px]">chevron_right</span>
    <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-label text-secondary">Cat III AIF</span>
    <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[12px]">chevron_right</span>
    <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-label text-on-surface">Long Only Funds</span>
  </div>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
      <span class="bg-secondary/10 text-secondary text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest px-3 py-1">Category III AIF</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="font-headline text-5xl md:text-6xl font-light leading-tight text-primary-container mb-4">
      Long Only <span class="italic">Funds</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed text-lg max-w-2xl">
      Concentrated equity ownership in exceptional businesses—disciplined quality investing without the constraint of benchmark-hugging mandates or hedging overlays.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Definition & Purpose -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <div class="bg-surface-container-low p-8 md:p-10 relative overflow-hidden">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl mb-6 text-primary-container">Definition & Purpose</h2>
      <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed mb-8">
        Long Only Funds under Category III AIF hold concentrated, purely long positions in listed equities without employing short selling, derivative hedging, or leverage. They represent the highest-conviction expression of fundamental equity research—portfolio managers identify a small number of high-quality businesses with durable competitive advantages and hold them through market cycles. Unlike mutual funds constrained by SEBI's position limits and diversification norms, AIFs can build materially larger stakes in individual companies, enabling a more meaningful alignment between investment thesis and portfolio weight.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-4">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-secondary mb-2 block">candlestick_chart</span>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-1">Focus</h4>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold">Listed Equities</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-4">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-secondary mb-2 block">monitoring</span>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-1">Risk Profile</h4>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold">High</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-4">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-secondary mb-2 block">payments</span>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-1">Min. Investment</h4>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold">&#8377;1 Crore</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-4">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-secondary mb-2 block">schedule</span>
          <h4 class="text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-1">Tenure</h4>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold">Open-Ended</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Key Characteristics -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-10 text-primary-container pl-4 border-l-2 border-tertiary-fixed">
      Key <span class="italic">Characteristics</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="space-y-8">
      <div class="flex gap-6 items-start">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-12 h-12 flex items-center justify-center bg-primary-container text-tertiary-fixed">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">trending_up</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-headline text-xl mb-2 text-on-surface">Pure Long Positions</h3>
          <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">The portfolio consists exclusively of long equity positions with no offsetting shorts, derivatives, or currency hedges. This construct delivers full upside participation in equity markets while accepting full drawdown risk during broad market corrections. The manager's skill is expressed entirely through stock selection and position sizing rather than hedging mechanics.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-6 items-start">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-12 h-12 flex items-center justify-center bg-primary-container text-tertiary-fixed">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">star</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-headline text-xl mb-2 text-on-surface">Alpha Generation Through Concentration</h3>
          <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Leading Long Only AIF managers maintain portfolios of 15 to 25 high-conviction positions, significantly more concentrated than mutual fund diversification requirements. This concentration amplifies the impact of individual stock selection decisions on overall fund performance, enabling meaningful outperformance relative to the benchmark when research is superior but demanding rigorous fundamental analysis to manage position risk.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-6 items-start">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-12 h-12 flex items-center justify-center bg-primary-container text-tertiary-fixed">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">block</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-headline text-xl mb-2 text-on-surface">No Hedging Constraint</h3>
          <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">The absence of hedging is a deliberate philosophical position, not a limitation. Long Only managers believe that the cost of systematic hedging—in both direct premium outlay and opportunity cost of portfolio construction constraints—exceeds the protection it provides over full market cycles. Investor suitability for this structure requires tolerance for market-correlated drawdowns.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lifecycle -->
  <section class="mb-16 bg-primary-container p-8 md:p-12 overflow-hidden relative">
    <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-12 text-tertiary-fixed">The Long Only Fund <span class="italic">Lifecycle</span></h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
      <div>
        <div class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-3">Phase 01</div>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl text-tertiary-fixed mb-3">Research & Universe Screening</h3>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">Investment candidates are identified through systematic screening of financial quality metrics—return on equity, free cash flow conversion, and management capital allocation track records. Qualitative assessment of competitive moat depth and industry structure narrows the universe to a watchlist of continuously monitored businesses.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-3">Phase 02</div>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl text-tertiary-fixed mb-3">Portfolio Construction & Holding</h3>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">Positions are initiated at valuations offering a margin of safety to intrinsic value estimates. Portfolio weights reflect conviction level and position-level risk contribution. The fund's philosophy typically favors patient holding through volatility rather than tactical rotation, allowing compounding to work over extended time horizons.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-3">Phase 03</div>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl text-tertiary-fixed mb-3">Rebalancing & Exit</h3>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">Positions are exited when intrinsic value estimates are exceeded, when the original investment thesis is invalidated by competitive or management changes, or when superior opportunities demand capital reallocation. In open-ended structures, redemptions are managed through secondary market sales without disturbing core portfolio positions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Notable Benchmarks -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-8 text-primary-container">Institutional <span class="italic">Benchmarks</span></h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div class="bg-surface-container-low p-6 border-l-2 border-tertiary-fixed">
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl mb-2 text-on-surface">Marcellus Investment Managers</h3>
        <p class="text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-3">Consistent Compounders Portfolio</p>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">Marcellus is synonymous with India's quality-investing movement, managing concentrated long-only portfolios around its "Consistent Compounders" framework—selecting businesses with clean accounts, high return on capital, and revenue growth driven by genuine competitive strength. Their coffee-can investing philosophy resists the temptation to trade around earnings noise, seeking multi-decade compounding from Indian franchise businesses.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-surface-container-low p-6 border-l-2 border-tertiary-fixed">
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl mb-2 text-on-surface">Motilal Oswal AMC</h3>
        <p class="text-xs font-label uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary mb-3">QGLP Framework Pioneer</p>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">Motilal Oswal's AIF and PMS platforms apply the QGLP framework—Quality, Growth, Longevity, and Price—to construct focused equity portfolios. Their long-only AIF vehicles maintain portfolios of 20 to 25 businesses, emphasizing owner-operator management teams and industries with structural tailwinds. Performance attribution is disciplined around stock selection rather than sector rotation or market timing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <div class="bg-surface-container p-8 text-center border border-outline-variant/10">
    <h3 class="font-headline text-2xl mb-4 text-on-surface">Explore This Strategy</h3>
    <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm mb-8">Access detailed regulatory filings and performance metrics through our private concierge.</p>
    <a href="/partner" class="inline-block w-full md:w-auto py-4 px-10 bg-primary-container text-on-primary font-label text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] hover:bg-slate-800 transition-colors">
      Request Fund Prospectus
    </a>
  </div>

</div>

</BaseLayout>
